{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-86532","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119797","text":"T&R — Travel & RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-86533","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119798","text":"A FreeBSD distribution, assembled rather than installed."}]},{"id":"blk-86534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119799","text":"T&R is built from "},{"id":"spn-119800","marks":["bold"],"text":"FreeBSD 15 pkgbase"},{"id":"spn-119801","text":" — the base system as ~509 packages — so making a root filesystem is "},{"id":"spn-119802","marks":["code"],"text":"pkg -r <dir> install"},{"id":"spn-119803","text":". There is no source tree, no "},{"id":"spn-119804","marks":["code"],"text":"buildworld"},{"id":"spn-119805","text":" and no release tarballs. "},{"id":"spn-119806","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr.conf"},{"id":"spn-119807","text":" "},{"id":"spn-119808","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-119809","text":" the distro; "},{"id":"spn-119810","marks":["code"],"text":"build-image.sh"},{"id":"spn-119811","text":" is the mechanism and should not need editing to make a different flavour."}]},{"id":"blk-86535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119812","text":"Two flavours, the same system with and without a screen:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-86537","spans":[{"id":"spn-119813","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-86538","spans":[{"id":"spn-119814","text":"server ("},{"id":"spn-119815","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr.conf"},{"id":"spn-119816","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-86539","spans":[{"id":"spn-119817","text":"desktop ("},{"id":"spn-119818","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr-desktop.conf"},{"id":"spn-119819","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-86536","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-86540","spans":[{"id":"spn-119820","text":"golden image"}]},{"id":"blk-86541","spans":[{"id":"spn-119821","marks":["bold"],"text":"364 MB"}]},{"id":"blk-86542","spans":[{"id":"spn-119822","marks":["bold"],"text":"~5.2 GB"}]}],[{"id":"blk-86543","spans":[{"id":"spn-119823","text":"packages"}]},{"id":"blk-86544","spans":[{"id":"spn-119824","text":"50"}]},{"id":"blk-86545","spans":[{"id":"spn-119825","text":"~350"}]}],[{"id":"blk-86546","spans":[{"id":"spn-119826","text":"what you get"}]},{"id":"blk-86547","spans":[{"id":"spn-119827","text":"sshd, cron, serial console"}]},{"id":"blk-86548","spans":[{"id":"spn-119828","text":"X.org, icewm + a vertical tint2 panel, Firefox, SDDM"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-86549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119829","text":"For comparison, FreeBSD's own cloud image is 2.51 GB with 504 packages, and a VM spawned from it writes ~3 GB to its overlay on first boot. A T&R server instance writes "},{"id":"spn-119830","marks":["bold"],"text":"51 MB"},{"id":"spn-119831","text":", because the image is already patched and does not re-download its own base every time it starts."}]},{"id":"blk-86550","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119832","text":"Build"}]},{"id":"blk-86551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119833","text":"The image must be assembled "},{"id":"spn-119834","marks":["bold"],"text":"on FreeBSD"},{"id":"spn-119835","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-119836","marks":["code"],"text":"makefs"},{"id":"spn-119837","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119838","marks":["code"],"text":"mkimg"},{"id":"spn-119839","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119840","marks":["code"],"text":"pkg -r"},{"id":"spn-119841","text":" are FreeBSD-native), so the build pushes this tree to a FreeBSD 15 builder over ssh and streams the result back. Any reachable FreeBSD machine with ~8 GB free will do:"}]},{"id":"blk-86552","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"BUILDER_SSH=root@10.0.0.5 ./make.sh tandr-desktop.conf"},{"id":"blk-86553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119842","text":"If "},{"id":"spn-119843","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/PARKVPS"}],"text":"PARKVPS"},{"id":"spn-119844","text":" is alongside, name one of its instances instead and the ssh details are looked up for you:"}]},{"id":"blk-86554","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"./make.sh tandr-desktop.conf builder"},{"id":"blk-86555","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119845","text":"What is in the box"}]},{"id":"blk-86556","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86558","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119846","marks":["bold"],"text":"Assembled from pkgbase."},{"id":"spn-119847","text":" Deliberately absent: "},{"id":"spn-119848","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-tests"},{"id":"spn-119849","text":" (~200 MB of"}]}],"id":"blk-86557","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119850","text":"test suites), every "},{"id":"spn-119851","marks":["code"],"text":"-dbg"},{"id":"spn-119852","text":" package, every "},{"id":"spn-119853","marks":["code"],"text":"lib32"},{"id":"spn-119854","text":" package."}]},{"id":"blk-86560","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119855","marks":["bold"],"text":"Serial console first."},{"id":"spn-119856","text":" "},{"id":"spn-119857","marks":["code"],"text":"comconsole,vidconsole"},{"id":"spn-119858","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-119859","marks":["code"],"text":"boot_multicons"},{"id":"spn-119860","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-86561","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119861","text":"because this image is built to be run headless by a supervisor and a guest that only talks to a framebuffer cannot be driven or logged."}]},{"id":"blk-86564","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86566","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119862","marks":["bold"],"text":"Root is found by GPT label, never device name."},{"id":"spn-119863","text":" "},{"id":"spn-119864","marks":["code"],"text":"vtbd0"},{"id":"spn-119865","text":" under virtio,"}]}],"id":"blk-86565","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119866","marks":["code"],"text":"ada0"},{"id":"spn-119867","text":" under SATA, "},{"id":"spn-119868","marks":["code"],"text":"nvd0"},{"id":"spn-119869","text":" under NVMe — a device-name fstab makes an image that only boots on the hypervisor it was built on."}]},{"id":"blk-86568","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86570","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119870","marks":["bold"],"text":"No `firstboot_pkg_upgrade`."},{"id":"spn-119871","text":" FreeBSD's own cloud images enable it, so every"}]}],"id":"blk-86569","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119872","text":"instance re-downloads ~512 MiB of base packages on first boot, forever. Patching is a build-time job done once."}]},{"id":"blk-86572","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86574","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119873","marks":["bold"],"text":"The desktop is themed as a cockpit"},{"id":"spn-119874","text":" — the palette comes from"}]}],"id":"blk-86573","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119875","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-119876","text":": amber "},{"id":"spn-119877","marks":["code"],"text":"#F2C14E"},{"id":"spn-119878","text":" for the focused window, cyan "},{"id":"spn-119879","marks":["code"],"text":"#2DE2E6"},{"id":"spn-119880","text":" for live readouts, bronze rims, on "},{"id":"spn-119881","marks":["code"],"text":"#03040a"},{"id":"spn-119882","text":". SDDM's greeter is a QML theme of its own with an "},{"id":"spn-119883","marks":["bold"],"text":"IGNITION"},{"id":"spn-119884","text":" button."}]},{"id":"blk-86576","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119885","text":"Things that will cost you a day if you rediscover them"}]},{"id":"blk-86577","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119886","text":"Written down because each one presents as something other than what it is."}]},{"id":"blk-86578","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119887","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-119888","marks":["code"],"text":"xorg-minimal"},{"id":"spn-119889","text":" installs font "},{"id":"spn-119890","marks":["italic"],"text":"libraries"},{"id":"spn-119891","text":" and zero font "},{"id":"spn-119892","marks":["italic"],"text":"files"},{"id":"spn-119893","text":".** A fontless"}]}],"id":"blk-86579","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119894","text":"icewm does not merely draw blank labels — it "},{"id":"spn-119895","marks":["bold"],"text":"stops moving windows"},{"id":"spn-119896","text":" (press, drag, release moves a window by exactly its decoration offset and no further), and fluxbox refuses to start at all. This reads as \"click and drag is broken\" and sends you through the whole input stack."}]},{"id":"blk-86582","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119897","marks":["bold"],"text":"A `usb-tablet` is mandatory for a usable desktop under VNC."},{"id":"spn-119898","text":" VNC speaks"}]}],"id":"blk-86583","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119899","marks":["italic"],"text":"absolute"},{"id":"spn-119900","text":" pointer positions; with only a PS/2 mouse the hypervisor converts them to relative motion and press/move/release land in three different places."}]},{"id":"blk-86586","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119901","marks":["bold"],"text":"`QtVersion=6` in an SDDM theme's `metadata.desktop` is load-bearing."}]}],"id":"blk-86587","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119902","text":"Without it SDDM 0.21 looks for the Qt5 greeter, does not find it, and falls back to its default theme. It looks exactly like a wrong theme name."}]},{"id":"blk-86590","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119903","marks":["bold"],"text":"The icewm package ships three xsession entries of its own"},{"id":"spn-119904","text":", and a greeter"}]}],"id":"blk-86591","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119905","text":"picks among them by sort order — so the panel silently never starts."}]},{"id":"blk-86594","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119906","marks":["bold"],"text":"icewm colours must live in a theme file"},{"id":"spn-119907","text":", not in "},{"id":"spn-119908","marks":["code"],"text":"~/.icewm/preferences"},{"id":"spn-119909","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-86595","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119910","text":"a loaded theme overrides that file and colours set there do nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-86598","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119911","text":"**tint2's "},{"id":"spn-119912","marks":["code"],"text":"panel_size"},{"id":"spn-119913","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-119914","marks":["code"],"text":"width height"},{"id":"spn-119915","text":" horizontally and "},{"id":"spn-119916","marks":["italic"],"text":"swapped"}]}],"id":"blk-86599","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119917","text":"vertically.** A 62 px full-height column is "},{"id":"spn-119918","marks":["code"],"text":"100% 62"},{"id":"spn-119919","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-86602","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119920","marks":["bold"],"text":"FreeBSD sets `schg` on parts of base"},{"id":"spn-119921","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-119922","marks":["code"],"text":"rm -rf"},{"id":"spn-119923","text":" cannot clean a staged"}]}],"id":"blk-86603","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119924","text":"root. "},{"id":"spn-119925","marks":["code"],"text":"chflags -R noschg"},{"id":"spn-119926","text":" first."}]},{"id":"blk-86606","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86608","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119927","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-119928","marks":["code"],"text":"pkg -r"},{"id":"spn-119929","text":" resolves trust against the "},{"id":"spn-119930","marks":["italic"],"text":"target"},{"id":"spn-119931","text":" root**, so an empty directory"}]}],"id":"blk-86607","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119932","text":"has no signing keys and fails with \"Error opening the trusted directory\" — which reads like a network fault."}]},{"id":"blk-86610","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119933","marks":["bold"],"text":"Four base packages look optional and are not"},{"id":"spn-119934","text":": "},{"id":"spn-119935","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-rc"},{"id":"spn-119936","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-119937","marks":["code"],"text":"/etc/rc"}]}],"id":"blk-86611","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86613","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119938","text":"at all), "},{"id":"spn-119939","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-ufs"},{"id":"spn-119940","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-119941","marks":["code"],"text":"fsck_ufs"},{"id":"spn-119942","text":", boot aborts), "},{"id":"spn-119943","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-geom"},{"id":"spn-119944","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-119945","marks":["code"],"text":"gpart"},{"id":"spn-119946","text":", needed by growfs), "},{"id":"spn-119947","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-utilities"},{"id":"spn-119948","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-119949","marks":["code"],"text":"awk"},{"id":"spn-119950","text":"). Plus "},{"id":"spn-119951","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-pam"},{"id":"spn-119952","text":" for sshd. The ssh package is "},{"id":"spn-119953","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-ssh"},{"id":"spn-119954","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-119955","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD-openssh"},{"id":"spn-119956","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-86614","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119957","text":"Logging in"}]},{"id":"blk-86615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119958","text":"The desktop flavour ships a user for the greeter, because root is refused for graphical login and the cloud-init user's password is locked. "},{"id":"spn-119959","marks":["bold"],"text":"The password is generated at build time"},{"id":"spn-119960","text":", printed once when the build finishes, and written to "},{"id":"spn-119961","marks":["code"],"text":"/root/DESKTOP-LOGIN"},{"id":"spn-119962","text":" and the MOTD inside the image. Set "},{"id":"spn-119963","marks":["code"],"text":"DESKTOP_PASSWORD"},{"id":"spn-119964","text":" in the config to pin one instead."}]},{"id":"blk-86616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119965","text":"Note the serial console is marked "},{"id":"spn-119966","marks":["code"],"text":"secure"},{"id":"spn-119967","text":" and root has no password, so anyone who can reach the console is root. That is fine for a disposable local VM and wrong the moment one listens on a real address."}]},{"id":"blk-86617","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119968","text":"Carrying the verifiable stack"}]},{"id":"blk-86618","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119969","text":"Set "},{"id":"spn-119970","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_DIST"},{"id":"spn-119971","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119972","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVS_DIST"},{"id":"spn-119973","text":" and the image ships TRVM and "},{"id":"spn-119974","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-119975","text":" — the runtime and the verifier that turns a run into a bundle somebody else can replay. Both are pure python against the standard library, so nothing is built on the target; "},{"id":"spn-119976","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-119977","text":", the native runtime, is C and is compiled "},{"id":"spn-119978","marks":["bold"],"text":"on the FreeBSD builder"},{"id":"spn-119979","text":", so the image gets a "},{"id":"spn-119980","marks":["code"],"text":"FreeBSD 15.1"},{"id":"spn-119981","text":" binary and still needs no compiler of its own."}]},{"id":"blk-86619","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"TRVM_DIST=../TRVM TRVS_DIST=../TRAAVIIS ./make.sh tandr.conf builder"},{"id":"blk-86620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119982","text":"Measured 2026-08-10, the same server config built both ways:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-86622","spans":[{"id":"spn-119983","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-86623","spans":[{"id":"spn-119984","text":"bare"}]},{"id":"blk-86624","spans":[{"id":"spn-119985","text":"+ stack"}]}],"id":"blk-86621","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-86625","spans":[{"id":"spn-119986","text":"image"}]},{"id":"blk-86626","spans":[{"id":"spn-119987","text":"363 MiB"}]},{"id":"blk-86627","spans":[{"id":"spn-119988","text":"625 MiB"}]}],[{"id":"blk-86628","spans":[{"id":"spn-119989","text":"packages"}]},{"id":"blk-86629","spans":[{"id":"spn-119990","text":"50"}]},{"id":"blk-86630","spans":[{"id":"spn-119991","text":"56"}]}],[{"id":"blk-86631","spans":[{"id":"spn-119992","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs doctor"}]},{"id":"blk-86632","spans":[{"id":"spn-119993","text":"not installed"}]},{"id":"blk-86633","spans":[{"id":"spn-119994","marks":["code"],"text":"status ready"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-86634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119995","text":"The stack is 14 MB of it. The rest is the interpreter, which is why "},{"id":"spn-119996","marks":["code"],"text":"python3"},{"id":"spn-119997","text":" lives in "},{"id":"spn-119998","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_PKGS"},{"id":"spn-119999","text":" rather than "},{"id":"spn-120000","marks":["code"],"text":"PORT_PKGS"},{"id":"spn-120001","text":" — a bare server should not pay 260 MB to ship sshd and cron, and an image without the stack has no "},{"id":"spn-120002","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-120003","text":" at all rather than one that exits "},{"id":"spn-120004","marks":["code"],"text":"python3: not found"},{"id":"spn-120005","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-86635","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120006","text":"Two sessions, and which one you get"}]},{"id":"blk-86636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120007","text":"With "},{"id":"spn-120008","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_DIST"},{"id":"spn-120009","text":" set, the image ships "},{"id":"spn-120010","marks":["bold"],"text":"two"},{"id":"spn-120011","text":" desktop sessions: the "},{"id":"spn-120012","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R cockpit"},{"id":"spn-120013","text":" (icewm + the panel) and "},{"id":"spn-120014","marks":["bold"],"text":"RRABBIT (the road)"},{"id":"spn-120015","text":". The greeter names the one it will start in the bottom-right corner, and "},{"id":"spn-120016","marks":["bold"],"text":"F2"},{"id":"spn-120017","text":" switches between them."}]},{"id":"blk-86637","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120018","text":"The default is the cockpit, and that is a decision the build writes down rather than an accident. A greeter picks among sessions by sort order, "},{"id":"spn-120019","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit.desktop"},{"id":"spn-120020","text":" sorts before "},{"id":"spn-120021","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr.desktop"},{"id":"spn-120022","text":", and measured on a fresh image SDDM duly preselected the 3D shell with no way to choose otherwise — which is the opposite of what "},{"id":"spn-120023","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-120024","text":" says it is for. The build now seeds SDDM's state file; set "},{"id":"spn-120025","marks":["code"],"text":"DEFAULT_SESSION=rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-120026","text":" in the config if you want the road on first login."}]},{"id":"blk-86638","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120027","text":"Name"}]},{"id":"blk-86639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120028","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R"},{"id":"spn-120029","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-120030","marks":["bold"],"text":"Travel & RRABBIT"},{"id":"spn-120031","text":" — two of them, with opposite appetites."}]},{"id":"blk-86640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120032","marks":["bold"],"text":"Travel"},{"id":"spn-120033","text":" wants to "},{"id":"spn-120034","marks":["italic"],"text":"navigate"},{"id":"spn-120035","text":". Travel is the one who drives: the road under you, the camera, the flight into a window and the chord back out, the districts you switch between. Travel's question is always "},{"id":"spn-120036","marks":["italic"],"text":"where am I, and how do I get to the other thing"},{"id":"spn-120037","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-86641","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120038","marks":["bold"],"text":"RRABBIT"},{"id":"spn-120039","text":" wants to "},{"id":"spn-120040","marks":["italic"],"text":"be the windows"},{"id":"spn-120041","text":". Not to display them — to be them. RRABBIT is the signs standing on the road, the surface that flattens to pixel-exact 1:1 under you, the rect in the ledger that decides whether a click belongs to it. RRABBIT's question is "},{"id":"spn-120042","marks":["italic"],"text":"what am I, and where do I stand"},{"id":"spn-120043","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-86642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120044","text":"Neither is much use alone. A navigator with nothing to navigate is a camera in an empty scene; windows with nobody driving are a desktop. The ampersand is the whole idea: "},{"id":"spn-120045","marks":["bold"],"text":"one likes going, the other likes being gone to."}]},{"id":"blk-86643","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120046","text":"The code does not make that split yet"}]},{"id":"blk-86644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120047","text":"Worth saying rather than implying otherwise. Today the two repositories are divided by "},{"id":"spn-120048","marks":["italic"],"text":"layer"},{"id":"spn-120049","text":", not by personality:"}]},{"id":"blk-86645","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120050","marks":["code"],"text":"travel-and-rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-120051","text":" (this repo) is the "},{"id":"spn-120052","marks":["bold"],"text":"distribution"},{"id":"spn-120053","text":" — the image, the"}]}],"id":"blk-86646","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86648","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120054","text":"boot path, the sessions. It carries Travel's name and is not Travel."}]},{"id":"blk-86649","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-86651","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120055","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/RRABBIT"}],"text":"`RRABBIT`"},{"id":"spn-120056","text":" holds "},{"id":"spn-120057","marks":["bold"],"text":"both halves"},{"id":"spn-120058","text":": the"}]}],"id":"blk-86650","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-86652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120059","text":"camera, flight and input that are Travel, and the surfaces, signs and ledger that are RRABBIT."}]},{"id":"blk-86653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120060","text":"So the name describes a separation the source has not made. That is a fair thing to notice and not obviously a fault — but anyone reading "},{"id":"spn-120061","marks":["code"],"text":"m2/shell.js"},{"id":"spn-120062","text":" looking for Travel will find them tangled, and should know that before going in."}]},{"id":"blk-86654","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120063","text":"The ampersand is a display name only"}]},{"id":"blk-86655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120064","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-120065","text":" is invalid in a hostname and needs quoting in every path that touches it, so "},{"id":"spn-120066","marks":["code"],"text":"DISTRO_SLUG"},{"id":"spn-120067","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-120068","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr"},{"id":"spn-120069","text":") is what filenames, the GPT label and the hostname are built from. Only prose gets the ampersand."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraxahodxayedfauaq7rn2td5prekvqvyr7yes4hsoxegl7lez45gra","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}